  "claim_limits": [
    "This is an implementation. Nothing was fitted for WTA01, no WTA target-year comparison was computed, and the real WTA01 comparison is the lead's to freeze and run. The calibration and selection stages the design requires do write score-like quantities; results.wta_smoke.score_bearing_artifacts names all four.",
    "Revision 2 left four review defects standing as known limits, recorded in references/WTA01_models/README.md: origins.json cites a revision label and not a commit (D6); the frozen cohort census is bound to the smoke run's feature table and not to each real configuration's own build (D8); the level rule admits one WTA 125 event and both year-end shapes (D9); and the sidecar DOB locator names a run-local path (D10).",
    "WTA 2007-2024 is exposed development data. The event crosswalk's surname classes and the WTA rule eras were both derived from outcome-bearing files.",
    "The WTA rule rows are inferred from the mirror's own deciding-set scores in the seasons they govern, target years included; they are not established as knowable at the declared cutoff. See wta_rules.json information_set_limit.",
    "The 13 winner-orientation conflicts, the 4 tennis-data-only matches, the 6 ambiguous pair keys, the 2 date defects and the 2 missing market dates are excluded and counted. None is resolved.",
    "Passing tests, a byte-identical ATP reproduction and a complete smoke run say the chain computes what is specified. They say nothing about whether the WTA sources are true or whether any WTA model is any good."
  ],
